# Approvals ledger — every human gate verdict, recorded where checks can read it.
# Format: date | scope | verbatim word | commit context
# Navigator-maintained; a gate's mechanical check may assert against this file.
#
# [Row 21] AND ONE NOW DOES, which is what this file was stood up for. A batch
# entry names its own directory in the scope column, and the last column is the
# commit the verdict was given against — `pending-close` or `-` while it is
# still open. `plan.spec` reads that: while an entry is open the batch it names
# must still be in the tree AND `approval.lock` must still carry its `pending`
# line, so the gate retires when a VERDICT is recorded here and not when a
# directory stops existing. Deleting the batch and the line together used to
# report five passes; now it reports a ledger entry with nothing under it.

